              "For gas targets, a small volume cell, 3.375-in. diam",
              "by 1.625 in. high, of 0.5-mil Dural, was used. The",
              "foils Au, Sn, Cu, Ni, and Al were of commercial",
              "origin. The Ag foil was prepared by",
              "electrodeposition. The Li foil (1 mil) was made by",
              "rolling Li metal with a glass roller under dry",
              "kerosene. The Li was then washed in n-decane and",
              "quickly put under vacuum. Scattering from any",
              "hydroxide layer on the Li could be resolved in the",
              "pulse-height analysis. The foil targets were about",
              "200 keV thick, the gas targets about 50 keV."
